<BaseLayout title="Realtime Data — Third-Party Exchange Access">
  <h3>Strategic Challenge</h3>
    <h3>Realtime data Pre-Auction Bidstream Access for Curators</h3>
      <p>
        Curators needed earlier access to auction-level signals in order to make informed buying decisions and activate curated demand strategies.
      </p>

      <p>
        The existing auction flow did not support <strong>pre-auction visibility or conditional deal activation</strong>,
        creating friction for curators and limiting participation in high-value inventory.
        The challenge was to enable <strong>controlled, real-time access to bidstream data</strong> without
        compromising auction performance, data integrity, or ecosystem trust.
      </p>

      <p>
        Solving this required rethinking <strong>auction sequencing, data exposure, and latency constraints</strong>,
        while preserving fairness and scalability across the exchange.
      </p>
<h3>Impact & Outcomes</h3>

<ul>
  <li>
    Enabled <strong>curated buyers to participate earlier in the auction lifecycle</strong>,
    increasing flexibility in how deals were activated and executed.
  </li>
  <li>
    Improved <strong>marketplace liquidity</strong> by allowing curators to selectively engage
    with inventory based on real-time auction signals.
  </li>
  <li>
    Preserved <strong>auction performance and fairness</strong> by introducing controlled,
    policy-aligned access to bidstream data.
  </li>
  <li>
    Created a <strong>scalable foundation for future real-time data products</strong>,
    supporting additional third-party integrations and advanced buying strategies.
  </li>
</ul>

    

</BaseLayout>
